{
  "version": 1,
  "_doc": "Real hockey drills for practices (docs/world/ON_ICE.md 4). Coordinates are [u, v] in the drill's area: u -1..1 along the ice (+u is the way the drill attacks), v -1..1 across it. 'full' drills want the whole ice, 'zone' an end zone or a pee-wee third, 'station' a quarter of a zone. A path point is [u, v, acts]; v '*' keeps the skater's own start lane. Travel acts: fast, slow, back (skate backwards), cross (crossovers), catch (wants a pass). Arrival acts: stop (hockey stop), pivot (forward/backward switch), mohawk (open-hip turn), shoot, pass_next (to the next lane's skater in the wave), pass_coach, call (the feeder passes them a puck), take (pick up a puck there), wait:N. Types: lanes, battle, game, tag, signal, circles. wave: together (one from every lane at once), alternate (one lane at a time), all (everyone at once).",
